Types: deb
URIs: https://packages.mozilla.org/apt
Suites: mozilla
Components: main
Signed-By: /etc/apt/keyrings/mozilla.gpg
Enabled: yes

# Firefox, as a real Debian package.
#
# PuralvOS has no snap (see excludes.list, "NO SNAP"). That has a cost: on
# Ubuntu 26.04 the `firefox` package in the Ubuntu archive is a *transitional
# wrapper* whose entire job is to install the snap. Removing snapd therefore
# removes the browser, and purging the archive's `firefox` deb does not bring
# it back.
#
# Alv and Puria use Firefox, so it has to come from somewhere real. Mozilla
# maintains an apt repository at packages.mozilla.org: upstream-built debs,
# signed by Mozilla's own key, updated on Mozilla's release schedule.
#
# This is a third-party repository and that is a real cost, stated rather than
# glossed over:
#
#   * It is a second archive to trust, pin by key, and update. Two archives
#     means two things that can break the build and one more signature to
#     verify. tools/manifest.py tracks what comes from where so that stays
#     visible.
#   * It is NOT a snap. It is an ordinary .deb installed by apt, pinned by
#     version like everything else, removable with apt, and updatable by the
#     same curated upgrade path as every other package in the image. That is
#     the whole reason for using it.
#   * If Mozilla ever stops publishing for a given Ubuntu release, the build
#     breaks loudly at apt-get update rather than silently shipping a browser
#     nobody can update.
#
# The alternative, if this ever goes wrong, is not "go back to snap". It is
# chromium from the Ubuntu archive, which is a real deb and is already in the
# archive PuralvOS trusts.